    {
      "api": "-[AVSpeechSynthesizer speakUtterance:]",
      "kind": "method",
      "introduced": "7.0",
      "minimum": "6.0",
      "status": "implemented",
      "facts": "facts/AVFoundation/AVSpeech.md",
      "reason": "the queue is the port's: the release's synthesizer replaces a string that is started while another speaks, so the port sends one string at a time",
      "source": "SDK 16.4, AVFAudio; tests/backports/host/avf-speech/synth-checks.m"
    },
    {
      "api": "-[AVSpeechSynthesizer stopSpeakingAtBoundary:]",
      "kind": "method",
      "introduced": "7.0",
      "minimum": "6.0",
      "status": "implemented",
      "facts": "facts/AVFoundation/AVSpeech.md",
      "reason": "the release's stop answers nil or an error, not a flag: the port answers YES while speaking and NO otherwise, from its own state",
      "source": "SDK 16.4, AVFAudio; tests/backports/host/avf-speech/synth-checks.m"
    },
    {
      "api": "-[AVSpeechSynthesizer pauseSpeakingAtBoundary:]",
      "kind": "method",
      "introduced": "7.0",
      "minimum": "6.0",
      "status": "implemented",
      "facts": "facts/AVFoundation/AVSpeech.md",
      "reason": "the port answers YES while speaking and NO otherwise, and a pause while paused answers YES, as the host does; the release's word-boundary pause lands one or two words after the call on the guest (the host's at the next word), measured in facts/AVFoundation/AVSpeech.md",
      "source": "SDK 16.4, AVFAudio; tests/backports/host/avf-speech/synth-checks.m"
    },
